WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.390
A site is often built in one place and run in another.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:09.305
The Deployment module moves configuration and content between Orchard Core sites.

00:00:09.305 --> 00:00:13.711
In this video, you build a deployment plan, export a package, and import

00:00:13.711 --> 00:00:15.180
it on a second site.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.525
You shape a site on one copy, with content types, settings, and pages.

00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:28.707
When that work is ready, a second site needs the same result.

00:00:28.707 --> 00:00:34.950
Repeating every change by hand takes time, and a forgotten setting makes the two sites differ.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.938
The Deployment module carries that work in a package.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.889
You describe what to include in a deployment plan, run the plan to

00:00:42.889 --> 00:00:46.620
produce the package, and import the package on the other site.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:50.043
A package is a zip file that holds a recipe.

00:00:50.043 --> 00:00:53.731
A recipe is a list of steps, and the destination site runs them

00:00:53.731 --> 00:00:56.030
in order when you import the package.

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:04.015
Deployment is a feature, listed under Tools, Features.

00:01:04.015 --> 00:01:07.665
Let's search for Deployment, which shows as Enabled.

00:01:07.665 --> 00:01:12.007
The Blog recipe enables it, and on a site where it is disabled,

00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:14.209
an Enable button turns it on.

00:01:14.668 --> 00:01:19.983
The Tools, Deployments menu lists Plans, which builds and runs plans, Package Import,

00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:24.305
which brings in a package, and JSON Import, which runs a recipe that

00:01:24.305 --> 00:01:25.998
you enter in an editor.

00:01:25.998 --> 00:01:31.898
Remote Instances and Remote Clients belong to Remote Deployment, which a separate video covers.

00:01:36.109 --> 00:01:37.998
This is the source site.

00:01:37.998 --> 00:01:41.209
Under Settings, General, the Page size is 25.

00:01:41.209 --> 00:01:45.994
A second site, the staging site, uses a different value, so let's move

00:01:45.994 --> 00:01:48.639
this setting with a deployment plan.

00:01:49.097 --> 00:01:53.941
The Plans page lists the deployment plans of the site, and this site has none.

00:01:53.941 --> 00:01:58.267
A plan is a named list of steps, so let's select Add Deployment Plan.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.125
A plan needs a name.

00:02:00.125 --> 00:02:04.900
Let's type Staging Setup and select Create, and the plan opens with no steps in it.

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:08.039
Add Step opens the Available Steps list.

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:13.404
Categories on the left group the steps, such as Configuration, Content Management, and

00:02:13.404 --> 00:02:16.377
Deployment, and each card describes its step.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:22.274
Modules that export data add their own steps, so the list depends on the enabled features.

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:27.204
Let's choose the Configuration category and select Add on the Site Settings card.

00:02:27.662 --> 00:02:31.509
The editor lists the site settings, each with a check box.

00:02:31.509 --> 00:02:34.214
Let's check PageSize and select Create.

00:02:34.214 --> 00:02:38.482
The plan shows the step, with PageSize as the setting it exports.

00:02:38.937 --> 00:02:41.602
Execute opens the Available Targets list.

00:02:41.602 --> 00:02:48.007
The Deployment module provides File Download, and Remote Deployment adds a target for each remote instance.

00:02:48.007 --> 00:02:49.877
Let's select File Download.

00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:53.759
The browser downloads a zip file named after the plan.

00:02:53.759 --> 00:02:57.642
It holds the recipe that the steps of the plan produced, so it

00:02:57.642 --> 00:02:59.983
is ready to import on another site.

00:03:04.168 --> 00:03:09.618
This is the staging site, a second Orchard Core site with the Deployment feature enabled.

00:03:09.618 --> 00:03:12.543
Under Settings, General, its Page size is 10.

00:03:12.543 --> 00:03:14.608
Let's import the package here.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.244
Under Tools, Deployments, let's open Package Import.

00:03:18.244 --> 00:03:22.029
The Select a file field accepts a zip package or a recipe file,

00:03:22.029 --> 00:03:25.211
so let's choose the zip file that the plan produced.

00:03:25.665 --> 00:03:29.814
Selecting Import runs the package right away, and the site runs the steps

00:03:29.814 --> 00:03:31.338
of the recipe in order.

00:03:31.338 --> 00:03:34.805
The page then shows the message Deployment package imported.

00:03:35.259 --> 00:03:39.947
Back under Settings, General, the Page size is 25, the value that the

00:03:39.947 --> 00:03:42.509
plan exported from the source site.

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:49.857
The Deployment module defines three permissions:

00:03:49.857 --> 00:03:55.219
Manage deployment plans covers creating and editing plans and their steps, Export Data

00:03:55.219 --> 00:03:59.300
covers running a plan, and Import Data covers both import pages.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.729
The Plans page needs the first two, and administrators have all three.

00:04:04.479 --> 00:04:09.099
When you edit a role, Import Data carries a Security Critical badge.

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:14.841
A recipe can change settings, features, content definitions, and content, so grant the

00:04:14.841 --> 00:04:20.459
permission only to roles you trust, and import only packages from sources you trust.

00:04:22.459 --> 00:04:26.356
Deployment moves configuration and content between sites:

00:04:26.356 --> 00:04:29.571
build a plan, export a package, and import it.

00:04:29.571 --> 00:04:34.271
Separate videos cover plans, imports, and remote deployment in detail.

00:04:34.271 --> 00:04:35.879
Thanks for watching.

